一座高铁站怎么运转 How a High-Speed Station Works — Miniature (微缩景观), a NEO-Cine library demo

THE STATION IS ILLUSTRATIVE: a fictional, typical Chinese high-speed rail station with no name. It does not represent any
real station, shows no operator's logo, livery, lettering or signage (signs are colour blocks and pictograms drawn in code),
and is not made, endorsed or checked by China State Railway Group or any operator. The layout (station building beside the
tracks, overpass in, underpass out, one island platform) is a diagram with compressed distances. Trains, cars and people run
on invented timings. The film prints no numbers; the procedures it names (real-name ID check, security check, ticket gates)
are sourced in FACTS.md. (The end card signs off with NEO-Cine only; this note is also at the top of DEMO.md.)

STYLE AND CODE: written for the NEO-Cine library from scratch. demo/kit/ (the miniature kit: bevelled geometry, plinth and
sections, parts, people, vehicles, lights, post, cameras, explainer layer, scene description builder), demo/station.js (the
scene description), demo/main.js (the film) and demo/mix.py (the sound). The style grammar learns from the general
traditions of architectural cut-away models, model railways and tilt-shift photography, and from the STYLE.md files of
Lemo-Opuscar's tilt-shift and white-model styles (MIT, (c) 2026 LemoLab); no code, design, palette or music is copied.

FACTS: see FACTS.md (Ministry of Transport regulations: 《铁路旅客车票实名制管理办法》 2022 No. 39; 《铁路旅客运输安全检查管理
  办法》 2023 No. 21, State Council Gazette). Checked 2026-11-14.

PICTURE: built entirely in code with three.js r170 (MIT): procedural geometry, RoomEnvironment reflections, three.js's GTAO
  and bloom passes, a tilt-shift blur written for this film. No photographs, scans, map data, AI-generated images, video or
  3D model files.

SOUND: all synthesized for this film in mix.py: kalimba, music-box and harp voices by the library's core/audio/pluck.py;
  marimba, glass bell, pads, rail rumble, brakes, chimes (a generic falling third, not any operator's chime), gate beeps,
  motors, clacks, paper, relay, hall murmur, birds and crickets in numpy and through core/audio/sfx.py. No samples or
  recordings.

FONTS (SIL Open Font License 1.1; fetched by tools/fonts.sh from github.com/google/fonts at commit 86aced91, not kept in git;
  licence texts in fonts/):
- Inter (variable, Inter[opsz,wght].ttf), The Inter Project Authors: Latin text and figures.
- Noto Sans SC (variable, NotoSansSC[wght].ttf), Google / Adobe: Chinese text, subset by tools/subset.py to the characters
  the film uses (fonts/NotoSansSC-sub.ttf).

TOOLS: the NEO-Cine library's core/ tools, which are Lemo-Opuscar's (MIT, (c) 2026 LemoLab): headless Chrome frame capture,
  events export, reading-time check, ffmpeg encode and loudness master; neo/audio/cues.py, neo/audio/master.py,
  neo/render/remote.sh. (neo/geo/buildings.py is supported by demo/kit/context.js for real places; this film uses no map data.)
